  "decision": "Re-evaluate every transition-advantage checkpoint with the intended beam objective: score a partial or completed beam only by the Energy of its terminal transition. Do not sum overlapping transition Energies. Reuse the completed cumulative curves as a negative control, the depth-1 score as the root-only control, and the existing distance-target curves because those already used terminal scoring. If H8 or H16 terminal scoring preserves or improves the strong depth-1 policy as depth increases, cumulative composition caused the apparent test-time scaling failure. If terminal scoring still collapses, the next audit must isolate predictor drift and intermediate beam pruning.",
